94,0$ a. (63) On leaves of Cyperaceae or Typha. Aerial hyphae without swellings,, not collapsing. ///Mat at first appressed to thinly downy, later developing white farinaceous lines or becoming thinly cottony to pellicular, white. Aerial hyphae thin- to firm-walled. Clamps variable in size. North-temperate. Ref.: Boidin et al., 1968. ///Code: 1, (2), 3, (7), (8), 13, 14, 17, (18),21, 24, 30, (37), 39, (42), 44, 45, (50), 51, 52, 53, 54, 57, 82, 83, (89), (91), 95, (97), 99. $ Epithele typhae (Pers.) Pat. [p. 142]
