95,0$ a. (94) Submerged hyphae always thin-walled. On angiosperms. Ref.: Boidin, 1958a; Boidin et al., 1968. ///Code: 1, (2), 3, (7), (8), (11), 13, (14), (17), (19), 21, (22), 24, 30, (31), 39, (42), (44), 45, (50), 51, 52, 53, (54), 57, 80, 82, 83, 89, (94), 95, 98, (99), (100). $ Vuilleminia comedens (Nees ex Fr.) Maire / Vuilleminia megalospora (Bres.) Bourd. & Galz.
95,0$ b. Some submerged hyphae with thickened to thick walls. On angiosperms, rarely gymnosperms Ref.: Boidin, 1958a. ///Code: 1, 3, (7), (8), (11), 13, (14), (17), 21, (22), 24, (25), 30, (31), 39, (44), 45, 48, (57), (80), 82, 83, 89, (90), (93), 95, 99. $ Aleurodiscus cerrusatus (Bres.) Hˆhn. & Litsch.
96,97$ a. (93) Hyphae with thick or thickened walls present
96,99$ b. Hyphae thin- to firm-walled
97,0$ a. (96) Thick-walled hyphae abundant, 1.5-2.5 µm wide, regular cells very long (up to 800 µm or more). Plate covered in 2 weeks. ///Advancing zone appressed to raised, hyphae distant. Mat cottony, becoming cottony-woolly or somewhat floccose, finally subfelty to lacunose, white. Reverse becoming bleached. Marginal and aerial hyphae 1.5-4.5 µm wide. Submerged hyphae up to 5.5(-6.5) µm wide. On angiosperms. North-temperate. Ref.: Nobles, 1948; van der Westhuizen, 1963. ///Code: 1, 3, (6), (11), (12), (13), 14, 19, 21, 22, (24), 27, 30, 37, 39, 42, 45, (46), 48, 52, 53, (54), (83), 89,(93). $ Cerrena unicolor (Bull. ex Fr.) Murrill
97,98$ b. Thick-walled hyphae not abundant and often not regular, up to 4(-5) µm wide
98,0$ a. (97) Marginal hyphae 1.5-5 µm wide. Growth rate 20-40 mm. Tyrosinase present ///Advancing zone appressed, even to slightly bayed, [p. 143] hyphae distant. Mat downy to cottony, becoming pellicular, white to cream. Reverse unchanged to slightly darker. Aerial and submerged hyphae 1.5-5(-6.5) µm wide, with thin to thickened or thick walls, sometimes with swellings. On angiosperms. North-temperate. Ref.: Boidin, 1958a. ///Code: 1, 2, 3, (8), (9), (11), 13, 14, (15), 17, 21, 24, 30, (31), (38), 39, 42, 44, 45, 48, (50), 52, 53, (54), 80, 83, 89, 95, 97, 99. $ Radulomyces molaris (Chaill. apud Fr.) M. P. Christ.  / Syn.: Radulum rude (Pers.) Lund.  †  
98,0$ b. Marginal hyphae (2-)2.5-6.5(-9) µm wide. Growth rate 40-65 mm. Tyrosinase absent. ///Advancing zone raised or appressed, hyphae rather distant. Mat downy to woolly, becoming subfelty, white to cream, sometimes with greyish tinges. Reverse typically darker. Aerial hyphae (1-)1.5-6.5 µm wide, with thin to thickened walls, sometimes with swellings, often constricted at the septa. On angiosperms, very rarely gymnosperms. North-temperate. Ref.: Boidin, 1958a; Boidin et al., 1968. ///Code: 1, 3, (7), (11), (12), (13), (14), (17), 22, 24, 30, 31, (33), 38, 39, 44, 45, 48, (50), (51), 52, 53, 54, (55), (80), 82, 83, 89, (90), (94), 95, 98, 100. $ Laeticorticium roseum (Pers. ex Fr.) Donk
99,0$ a. (96) Growth rate up to 30 mm. Marginal hyphae 1-3(-4) µm wide. $ See Leptosporomyces galzinii under 72d
99,100$ b. Growth rate 35-55 mm (except sometimes Hypochnicium lundellii). Marginal hyphae (1-)2-5.5(-7) µm wide Advancing zone appressed, hyphae typically distant. Mat downy to thinly cottony or cottony-woolly, translucent, later often pellicular, white. Reverse unchanged to somewhat bleached. Aerial hyphae thin- to firm-walled, with clamps of variable size. 
100,0$ a. (99) Growth rate 35-50 mm. Mat rarely with plumose structures. Aerial hyphae 1.5-7 µm wide, often somewhat irregular in outline. On angiosperms and gymnosperms. North-temperate ///Code: 1, 3, (7), (8), (11), (12), (13), 14, 17, 21, 22, 24, 30, 39, 44, 45, 52, 53, 54, (80), 83, (89), (90), (94). $Hypochnicium bombycinum (Sommerf. ex Fr.) J. Erikss.
100,0$ b.* Growth rate 20-50 mm. Mat very thin, woolly to pellicular. [p. 144] Aerial hyphae 2-6 µm wide, often somewhat irregular. Submerged hyphae irregular, sometimes with swellings, often constricted at the septa, up to 7.5(-9.5) µm wide. Mainly on gymnosperms but also angiosperms. North-temperate. ///Code: 1, 3, (7), (8), (9), (12), (13), 14, (17), (21), 22, 24, 30, 39, 44, 45, 52, 53, 54, (55), (57), (80), 83, (89), (90), 95, 97. /// $ Hypochnicium lundellii (Bourd. apud J. Erikss.) J. Erikss.
100,0$ c.* Growth rate 3 5-5 5 mm. Mat thinly cottony to cottony-woolly, becoming pellicular. Aerial and submerged hyphae 2-7(-9) µm wide, some with one or more swellings (often terminal) up to 12 µm diam, with granular contents. Mainly on gymnosperms, also angiosperms. North-temperate. ///Code: 1, 3, (7), (8), (11), 13, 14, (16), (17), 21, 22, 24, 30, (37), 39, 44, 45, (50), 52, 53, 54, (55), 60, 80, 83, (89), (90), 95, 97. $ Hypochnicium punctulatum (Cooke) J. Erikss.  
100,0,n$ H. cystidiatum Boidin & Gilles as described by Boidin and Lanquetin (1971) also keys out here.
100,0$ d.* Growth rate 35-50 mm. Mat sometimes woolly to locally plumose, remaining thin. Aerial hyphae (1-)2-7 µm wide, some with narrow, much-branched hyphae. Submerged hyphae sometimes reaching 8 µm in width. On angiosperms. Temperate. ///Code: 1, (2), 3, (7), (8), (11), 13, 14, 17, 21, 22, (23), 24, 30, (37), 39, 42, 44, 45, (51), 52, 53, 54, (55), (57), 82, 83, (88), 89, (93), 95, 97, 99. $ Hyphoderma setigerum (Fr.) Donk  
