29,0$ a. (28) Colony becoming orange. Hyphae up to 4.5 µm wide, without swellings. ///Growth rate 2-5 mm on ChA; no growth on MEA. Advancing zone raised, even, hyphae dense. Mat cottony to cottony-woolly. Marginal and aerial hyphae 2-4(-4.5) µm wide. Chlamydospores abundant, subglobose to ellipsoid, (7-)9-15 x (4-)6-8(-10) µm, sometimes slightly irregular, thick-walled (wall up to 2.5 µm thick). On angiosperms, mainly Quercus. ///Code: 2, (10), 11, 12, 21, 22, (30), 32, (35), 39, 42, 44, 52, 53, 82, 83, 85, 89. $ Buglossoporus pulvinus (Pers.) Donk.  /Syn.: Buglossoporus quercinus (Schrad. ex Fr.) Kotl. & Pouzar 
