30,0$ a. (29) Growth rate -5-9 mm. Submerged hyphae up to 5.5 µm wide.///Advancing zone appressed, even, hyphae dense. Mat farinaceous to low cottony, white, becoming felty and Light Buff to Warm Buff. Reverse darker. Marginal and aerial hyphae (1.5-)2-3.5 µm wide, some with yellowish contents. Not all septa with clamps. Chlamydospores to ovoid, hyaline to brownish, [p. 155] 9-16.5(-21) x 5-11.5 µm. On gymnosperms. North-temperate. Ref.: Lombard and Gilbertson, 1965. ///Code: (10), (11), 13, 18, 21, 25, 30, 31, 35, 38, (39), (42), 44, 52, 53, (54), (67), (78), 80, 83, 85, (89), (90). $ Anomoporia bombycina (Fr.) Pouzar 
30,0$ b. Growth rate 35->70 mm. Submerged hyphae up to 8(-10) µm wide.///Advancing zone appressed, even to bayed, hyphae distant. Mat downy to thinly cottony, white, becoming pellicular to farinaceous-felty, often with cottony overgrowth which becomes cream to Naples Yellow or even Mustard Yellow, turning somewhat darker in KOH. Reverse unchanged to slightly darker. Marginal hyphae 2.5-6 µm wide. Aerial hyphae hyaline to yellowish, 2-5(-10) µm wide, often ampullate or with swellings, some encrusted with crystalline material. Chlamydospores subglobose to ellipsoid or ovoid, 10-19(-27.5) x 7-14 µm. North and central America. Ref.: Lombard and Gilbertson, 1965. ///Code: (4), (6), (7), (11), 13, 14, (15), 17, (18), 21, 24, 25, 30, 31, 35, (38), 39, 42, 44, 52, 53, 54, (55), 67, 78, 80, 82, 83, 85, (89), (90). $ Fibroporia radiculosa (Peck) Parm. 

31,32$ a. (30) Chlamydospores ellipsoid, about (1.5-)2 times as long as broad
31,34$ b. Chlamydospores (sub)globose to rarely broadly ellipsoid, rarely reaching a length-width ratio of 1.5

32,0$ a. Chlamydospores 20-26 x 6-11 µm. ///Advancing zone raised or appressed, even, hyphae rather distant. Mat cottony to cottony-woolly, becoming floccose-cottony (around the inoculum velvety), white. Marginal and aerial hyphae 1.5-4.6 µm. (Sub)tropical. Ref.: Bakshi et al., 1970. ///Code: (6), (7), (8), (11), (12), (13), (14), 19, 21, 22, 25, 30, 39, 42, (44), 45, 52, 53, 83, 85, 89. $ Trametes cubensis (Mont.) Sacc. 
