46,0$ a. (45) Growth rate 30-50 mm. Cystidia 6.5-11(-16) µm wide at the tip, often with thickened walls. ///Advancing zone appressed to submerged, hyphae distant. Mat appressed or locally pruinose to downy, whitish. Some fascicles present, especially around the inoculum. Marginal hyphae 1-2(-3) µm wide, sometimes irregular with swellings. Aerial hyphae 1-4 µm wide, with thin (in the fascicles with thickened) wall, rarely encrusted. Cystidia up to 40 µm long, apically often covered with resinous material. North-temperate. Ref.: Boidin, 1958a. ///Code: (1), 2, (3), (7), (8), 13, 14, (16), 17, (18), (23), (30), 39, 45, (48), 51, 52, 53, (57), 72, 80, (81), 95, 97. $ Xenasma pruinosum (Pat.) Donk  
