50,0$ a. (49) Hyphal swellings in chains, broadly ellipsoid to globose, up to 25 µm diam, separated by clamped septa ///Growth rate 2-4 mm. Advancing zone appressed, hyphae rather distant. Mat appressed to minutely downy, hyaline to whitish. Marginal, aerial and submerged hyphae 3-7(-12) µm wide, thin- to firm-walled, branching at right angles. Diameter of the clamps less than that of the hyphae. North-temperate. Ref.: Boidin, 1958a. ///Code: (1), (10), (11), 13, (14), (16), (17), (30), 39, 44, (48), 53, 54, 55, 79, (89), (90), 95, 97, 99. $ Botryobasidium subcoronatum (Hˆhn. & Litsch.) Donk   
