51,0$ a. (50) Growth rate not exceeding 6 mm, rarely reaching 20 mm in 6 weeks.///On gymnosperms. Crystals absent or much smaller. Swellings typically intercalary. $Two incompletely known species, described by Boidin (1958a) key out here: Clavulicium macounii (Burt) J. Erikss. & Boid. ex Parm. (/Syn.: Corticium pilatii Boid.) with swellings up to 25 µm diam and silky aerial mycelium in the centre of the mat and also Tubulicrinis subulatus (Bourd. & Galz.) Donk with swellings 4-6 µm diam.
