57,58,n$ The separation of cultures of the above two species is not possible with certainty. The thickwalled hyphae with meandering lumen are not typical for T. leucospongia, as stated by Bakshi et al. (1969). Fragmenting hyphal segments and poorer growth on MEA of T. fragilis may be distinctive characters, but this is far from certain. 
57,58$ b. Growth rate at least 13 mm. Hyphae with meandering lumen absent. 
57,0,n$ The strains of Tyromyces immitis (Peck) Bond isolated by Nobles and Robbins, a species considered by Domanski et al. (1967) as a /Synonym of T. stypticus (Pers. ex Fr.) Kotl. & Pouzar,, agree with strains of T. stypticus except for the slower growth rate which is 7-25 mm. See under 68b. 

